WEBVTT

00:00:10.177 --> 00:00:14.137
You have to get rid of it.
Today.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.578
Take my hand.

00:00:36.203 --> 00:00:38.683
The Room of Requirement.

00:00:44.515 --> 00:00:47.344
GINNY:
We need to hide
the Half-Blood Prince's book

00:00:47.388 --> 00:00:51.261
where no one will ever find it,
including you.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.268
[RUSTLING]

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.619
What was that?
What was that?

00:01:09.497 --> 00:01:12.413
[RUSTLING CONTINUES]

00:01:20.551 --> 00:01:22.553
[CHIRPING]

00:01:26.514 --> 00:01:28.864
See?

00:01:28.907 --> 00:01:31.127
You never know what you'll find
up here.

00:01:35.174 --> 00:01:37.176
[♪♪♪]

00:01:50.059 --> 00:01:54.193
All right, close your eyes.
That way you can't be tempted.

00:01:57.893 --> 00:02:00.025
[WHISPERING]
Close your eyes.

00:02:26.182 --> 00:02:29.316
That can stay hidden
up here too, if you like.

00:02:37.933 --> 00:02:39.935
[BIRD CHIRPING]

00:02:43.765 --> 00:02:46.245
So did you and Ginny do it,
then?

00:02:46.289 --> 00:02:47.638
What?

00:02:47.682 --> 00:02:49.814
You know, hide the book?

00:02:49.858 --> 00:02:51.990
Oh, yeah.

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:57.387
Ah. Dear, yes.

00:02:57.431 --> 00:03:00.390
Still no luck with Slughorn,
then, I take it?

00:03:02.218 --> 00:03:04.438
Luck.

00:03:04.481 --> 00:03:08.355
That's it.
All I need's a bit of luck.

00:03:26.068 --> 00:03:29.419
HERMIONE:
Well, how do you feel?

00:03:29.463 --> 00:03:32.204
Excellent.

00:03:32.248 --> 00:03:34.424
Really excellent.

00:03:36.513 --> 00:03:38.907
Remember,

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.909
Slughorn usually eats early,

00:03:40.952 --> 00:03:44.086
takes a walk,
and then returns to his office.

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:45.914
Right.

00:03:45.957 --> 00:03:48.351
I'm going down to Hagrid's.What?

00:03:48.395 --> 00:03:51.180
No, Harry, you've got to go
and speak to Slughorn.

00:03:52.573 --> 00:03:55.358
We have a plan.HARRY: I know,

00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:57.578
but I've got a good feeling
about Hagrid's.

00:03:57.621 --> 00:04:00.189
I feel i-it's the place to be
tonight.

00:04:00.232 --> 00:04:02.278
Do you know what I mean?

00:04:02.321 --> 00:04:03.627
BOTH: No.Well, trust me,

00:04:03.671 --> 00:04:07.849
I know what I'm doing.
Or Felix does.

00:04:07.892 --> 00:04:09.024
Hi!

00:04:38.314 --> 00:04:39.924
[GRUNTS]

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.883
Merlin's beard, Harry!

00:04:41.926 --> 00:04:44.276
Sorry, sir.
I should've announced myself.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.235
Cleared my throat, coughed.

00:04:46.278 --> 00:04:48.280
You probably feared
I was Professor Sprout.

00:04:48.324 --> 00:04:51.849
Yes, I did, actually.
What makes you think that?

00:04:51.893 --> 00:04:54.112
Well, just the general behavior,
sir.

00:04:54.156 --> 00:04:57.115
The sneaking around,
the jumping when you saw me.

00:04:57.159 --> 00:04:59.074
Are those Tentacula leaves,
sir?

00:04:59.117 --> 00:05:00.902
They're very valuable,
aren't they?

00:05:00.945 --> 00:05:03.382
Ten Galleons a leaf
to the right buyer.

00:05:03.426 --> 00:05:05.689
Not that I'm familiar
with any such transactions,

00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:07.212
but one does hear rumors.

00:05:07.256 --> 00:05:10.955
My own interests
are purely academic, of course.

00:05:10.999 --> 00:05:14.524
Personally, these plants
always kind of freaked me out.

00:05:14.568 --> 00:05:16.308
Mm.

00:05:17.658 --> 00:05:19.790
Exactly how did you get out
of the castle, Harry?

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.575
Through the front door,
sir.

00:05:21.618 --> 00:05:23.968
I'm off to Hagrid's.
He's a very dear friend

00:05:24.012 --> 00:05:25.753
and I just fancied
paying him a visit.

00:05:25.796 --> 00:05:28.277
So if you don't mind,
I will be going now.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.931
Harry!

00:05:31.323 --> 00:05:33.891
Sir?It's nearly nightfall.

00:05:33.935 --> 00:05:35.632
Surely you realize
I can't allow you

00:05:35.676 --> 00:05:37.634
to go roaming the grounds
by yourself.

00:05:37.678 --> 00:05:40.594
Well, then, by all means,
come along, sir.

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.032
[♪♪♪]

00:05:45.424 --> 00:05:48.906
Harry, I must insist
you accompany me

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.821
back to the castle
immediately!

00:05:50.865 --> 00:05:54.216
That would be counterproductive,
sir.

00:05:55.304 --> 00:05:58.568
And what makes you
say that?

00:05:58.612 --> 00:06:00.483
No idea.

00:06:06.924 --> 00:06:08.926
Horace.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.494
SLUGHORN:
Merlin's beard.

00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:14.802
Is that an actual
Acromantula?

00:06:14.845 --> 00:06:17.674
A dead one,
I think, sir.

00:06:17.718 --> 00:06:19.546
Good God.

00:06:19.589 --> 00:06:23.332
Dear fellow, however did you
manage to kill it?

00:06:23.375 --> 00:06:26.857
Kill it?
Me oldest friend, he was.

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.380
I'm so sorry,
I didn't--

00:06:28.424 --> 00:06:31.514
Oh, don't worry yourself,
you're not alone.

00:06:31.558 --> 00:06:35.213
Seriously misunderstood
creatures, spiders are.

00:06:35.257 --> 00:06:37.651
It's the eyes, I reckon.
They unnerve some folk.

00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:39.957
Not to mention the pincers.

00:06:40.001 --> 00:06:42.046
[CLICKING TONGUE]

00:06:44.135 --> 00:06:46.877
Yeah, I reckon that too.

00:06:46.921 --> 00:06:50.272
Hagrid, the last thing
I wish to be is indelicate,

00:06:50.315 --> 00:06:54.493
but Acromantular venom
is uncommonly rare.

00:06:54.537 --> 00:06:57.061
Would you allow me
to extract a vial or two?

00:06:57.105 --> 00:06:59.716
Purely for academic purposes,
you understand.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.806
Well, I don't suppose it's going
to do him much good now, is it?

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.286
My thoughts exactly.

00:07:04.329 --> 00:07:08.333
Always have a ampoule or two
about my person

00:07:08.377 --> 00:07:10.901
for just such occasions as this.

00:07:10.945 --> 00:07:13.208
Old, uh,

00:07:13.251 --> 00:07:16.733
Potions Master's habit,
you know.

00:07:16.777 --> 00:07:19.257
I wish you could've seen him
in his prime.

00:07:19.301 --> 00:07:23.174
Magnificent, he was.
Just magnificent.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.569
Oh, dear.

